Hi Andreas,

On 16-09-2021 17:33, Andreas Tille wrote:
> I wonder whether there is an easy method to obtain all those packages
> with names r-bioc-* failing its test in unstable.

We don't perform archive wide testing of unstable anymore as targeted
testing is so much more interesting. What I suggest for your case is to
use the API [1], schedule a test run of all the packages you want to
know the status of (preferable on one arch only, best is arm64), query
*your* results (automatically done if you schedule and query using the
API) and check which packages fail. The results of the API come in json
format so should be extremely easy to process.

Paul

[1] https://ci.debian.net/api/doc

